WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.335 --> 00:00:02.143
- Just sitting at my desk at home

00:00:02.143 --> 00:00:05.976
when I stabbed myself
with a pencil in my eye.

00:00:11.118 --> 00:00:13.920
- I was in the first grade,
and I was six years old.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:14.800
- Second grade.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.435
- Probably the third grade.

00:00:16.435 --> 00:00:18.232
- Third grade or fourth grade.

00:00:18.232 --> 00:00:19.679
- I was in seventh grade.

00:00:19.679 --> 00:00:22.020
- This is the first time
I've told this story

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:25.390
because it just doesn't
come up that often.

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:28.281
- My friend and I had been
messing around a little bit,

00:00:28.281 --> 00:00:31.555
and I had elbowed him in the leg.

00:00:31.555 --> 00:00:33.489
So, we were sitting in the wood shop

00:00:33.489 --> 00:00:36.304
with a very attentive teacher.

00:00:36.304 --> 00:00:38.679
As soon as he turned around, my buddy

00:00:38.679 --> 00:00:41.200
took his mechanical
pencil and just kind of

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.950
gave me a quick jab in the thigh.

00:00:47.357 --> 00:00:50.151
- So I was walking to one of my classes.

00:00:50.151 --> 00:00:54.212
In our school, there was
brick wall everywhere.

00:00:54.212 --> 00:00:56.153
And I had my pencil in my hand.

00:00:56.153 --> 00:00:58.414
I was dragging it along the brick wall.

00:00:58.414 --> 00:01:00.575
And it got wedged in between a brick,

00:01:00.575 --> 00:01:04.242
and then the pencil
went right into my hand.

00:01:08.509 --> 00:01:10.370
- I was sitting at the kitchen table,

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:11.787
and I was coloring.

00:01:11.787 --> 00:01:16.070
And I like to take a regular pencil first.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:19.421
And I was erasing, and it jabbed right in.

00:01:19.421 --> 00:01:21.484
It got lodged right in there,
and I started to scream

00:01:21.484 --> 00:01:23.255
'cause it hurts really, really, really bad

00:01:23.255 --> 00:01:25.421
when you get anything
in between your fingers.

00:01:25.421 --> 00:01:27.398
I thought I was gonna get lead poisoning

00:01:27.398 --> 00:01:31.565
'cause I didn't understand
that it's not poisonous.

00:01:33.185 --> 00:01:35.255
- My younger brother and
I were farting around

00:01:35.255 --> 00:01:36.171
in the living room.

00:01:36.171 --> 00:01:40.322
And I don't know why, but
he had sharpened a pencil,

00:01:40.322 --> 00:01:42.657
tossed willy-nilly onto the floor.

00:01:42.657 --> 00:01:44.640
And I'm running around
without my shoes on.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.512
Step on it, crack, ugh.

00:01:46.512 --> 00:01:50.156
It had stuck into the
bottom of my left foot.

00:01:50.156 --> 00:01:51.837
And I tried to get it out.

00:01:51.837 --> 00:01:53.323
The more I tried to dig it out,

00:01:53.323 --> 00:01:57.490
the further it seemed to
enmesh itself with my flesh.

00:01:59.975 --> 00:02:02.389
- I was just sitting at my desk at home.

00:02:02.389 --> 00:02:04.855
And I must have just erasing
something really vigorously,

00:02:04.855 --> 00:02:06.823
gesturing a little bit
too hard, and it went

00:02:06.823 --> 00:02:08.289
straight into my eye.

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:10.239
I just immediately started freaking out

00:02:10.239 --> 00:02:12.701
'cause I could see the
mark it left in my eye.

00:02:12.701 --> 00:02:15.660
And I was like, "Oh, my
God, am I gonna go blind?"

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:17.258
- People have totally
noticed it without me

00:02:17.258 --> 00:02:20.093
sharing the information because it's like

00:02:20.093 --> 00:02:22.431
in the center of my right hand.

00:02:22.431 --> 00:02:23.978
There is a black dot.

00:02:23.978 --> 00:02:26.145
It's buried under my skin.

00:02:27.794 --> 00:02:29.009
- Now it's just a part of me.

00:02:29.009 --> 00:02:31.568
I'm kind of a cyborg in that sense.

00:02:31.568 --> 00:02:33.727
- It's actually funny because
I'm the type of person

00:02:33.727 --> 00:02:36.092
that has never broken any sort of bone.

00:02:36.092 --> 00:02:37.562
So now that I think of
it, this is probably

00:02:37.562 --> 00:02:40.498
the worst battle scar I honestly have

00:02:40.498 --> 00:02:43.476
is just this thing in my eye

00:02:43.476 --> 00:02:45.551
from stabbing myself with a pencil.

00:02:45.551 --> 00:02:49.014
- I just hope somebody out
there can hear my story

00:02:49.014 --> 00:02:51.679
and feel better about
their pencil stabbing.

00:02:51.679 --> 00:02:53.827
- So for anyone who thinks that
they're alone in this world

00:02:53.827 --> 00:02:55.625
with their pencil scars, you're not.

00:02:55.625 --> 00:02:57.267
- There are a lot of us out there.

00:02:57.267 --> 00:03:01.478
And if you ever feel lonely,
you can probably find

00:03:01.478 --> 00:03:03.551
support on an internet forum.

00:03:03.551 --> 00:03:05.212
I'm sure they exist.

00:03:05.212 --> 00:03:07.456
- You should wear it proudly.

00:03:07.456 --> 00:03:10.111
And just show that you
can move on from this.

00:03:10.111 --> 00:03:14.278
- Or just find me on Twitter,
and I'll commiserate.

